// pm/lines/firepit.js — the host and the texts around the fire pit, and the
// ballots read out at it (pm/moments.js, arrivals.js, casa.js). Data only.
//
// What still plays from the old pools (the 2026-10-22 rebuild moved every
// conversation to pm/talk/): the host's lines, which say exactly how each
// night's format works and never a word ahead of the result she reads; the
// texts, which do the same; and one-sentence ballots, which is what a vote is.
//   host-open        []          night one: Dior opens the show
//   host-first       []          Dior explains the first coupling. `of`: the format
//   date-text        [a, b, (c)] a reads the text: dates with b (and c). `of`: one · two
//   nobody-stands    [a]         new arrival a asks, and nobody stands
//   rule-open        [a]         a bombshell night's rule, said before it plays. `of`: stand-up · public-matches
//   casa-host        []          the host opens the Casa Amor return
//   casa-explain     []          the host explains Casa. `of`: f · m (who goes)
//   dump-text        [a, (b)]    the text that there is a dumping tonight. `of`: the format
//   dump-open        []          the host says exactly how tonight works. `of`: the format
//   dump-recap       [a, b, (c)] the host on a moment since the last dumping. `of`: its kind, or intro; `ago`
//   dump-buildup     [a, b]      a couple at risk. `nth`: first · next · only
//   dump-at-risk     [a]         a alone is at risk
//   dump-safe        [a, b]      a safe couple, read out. `nth`: first · next · last
//   dump-decide      []          the host hands the decision over. `of`: the format
//   dump-verdict     [a]         a is dumped. `channel`: public · villa · recoupling · casa
//   dump-verdict-couple [a, b]   a and b are dumped together
//   dump-verdict-singles [a, b…] everyone left single goes; {a} and {b} the first two
//   dump-fallout     [a]         a is suddenly single
//   ballot-reveal    [a, b]      a stands and votes to dump b
//   save-vote        [a, b]      a votes to SAVE b
//   top-couple-pick  [a, b, c, d] the public's favourite couple a and b send c and d home
//   couples-vote     [a, b, c, d] a and b name c and d the least compatible
//   ex-return        [a]         the dumped islanders walk back in to vote, led by a
//   ex-ballot        [a, b]      ex-islander a votes against b's couple. `grudge`: voted · moved-on
//   vote-safe        [a, b]      the text: nobody goes tonight
//   recouple-text    [a, (b)]    the text: a recoupling. `of`: f · m (who chooses)
//   recouple-open    []          the host: who chooses (`of` f/m), and the stake (all · risk · safe)
//   recouple-first   [a, …]      the first to choose. `of`: many · few
//   recouple-single  [a]         a is left single. `of`: vulnerable · kept
//   movie-night      [a, b…]     a clip of a (and b) plays; {quote} is its line
